findings.detail:
classifyCi throws on many conditions, for example:
- a non-200 REST read;
- zod parse errors;
- `Ambiguous originating CI job`;
- `Incomplete failing check`;
- `Incomplete CI log`.

`record()` awaits it without a try/catch. The error propagates out of the per-PR loop in `observe()`, and `tick` only logs it. `record` saves `ciPending: true` before calling classifyCi, so the same PR throws again on every poll. Every PR after it in the batch is then never recorded, so state changes, `pr.merged` and merge reconciliation are all missed, as is the nudge for the failing PR itself.
